# Renderer (Vite) build-time variables for the sync agent desktop app.
#
# Vite reads THIS file — the repo root, beside vite.config.ts. It does NOT read
# server/.env, which is a different file for a different process. That is the
# whole bug this file fixes: the root .env did not exist, so both variables were
# undefined at build time and the packaged renderer shipped with NO Supabase read
# client. The Supabase Cloud panel said so honestly ("no read client... empty here
# means could not ask, not nothing has synced") and the history and push-log lists
# stayed permanently empty while pushing worked fine.
#
# Both values are PUBLISHABLE and RLS-gated by design — the web app ships the same
# pair in a public bundle. They are inlined into the JS at build time, so changing
# this file requires a rebuild; editing a .env on a user machine does nothing.
#
# The service-role key does NOT belong here and must never be given a VITE_ prefix:
# anything VITE_ is compiled into the renderer and is therefore public.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<publishable key from Supabase → Project Settings → API>
